# Dockerfile.dockerignore — build context filter for demo/agui_web.
#
# Docker picks this up automatically because it sits next to the Dockerfile and
# is named <Dockerfile>.dockerignore; building with an explicit -f is what
# activates it.
#
# The context is the repository root, which holds .git, scratch checkouts under
# tmp/, and apps/.env with real provider credentials. This image needs none of
# it: the agent is a local function graph, so no key ever enters the build.
#
# One syntax rule, learned the hard way on demo/6_adk_telegram_bot: a negated
# DIRECTORY pattern re-admits everything under it, because a leading `**` matches
# at every depth and a parent's own entry governs its children. `!demo/` would
# admit every demo in the tree, so the exact directory is named instead.

# Exclude everything, then re-admit only what the two binaries import.
**
!go.mod
!go.sum

!internal/
!week2/internal/refund/
!week2/Day4_Agent_as_Service_Deploy/labs4/
!demo/agui_web/

# Defence in depth for the file that must never reach a layer, a build cache or
# a registry. apps/.env is already git-ignored and excluded above; this line
# means a future `!apps/` cannot quietly undo that.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Not compiled, not needed to build the binaries, so the context stays the source
# that actually ships. main_test.go is included deliberately: this demo has no
# tests yet, and the pattern is here so adding one does not enlarge the context.
**/*_test.go
**/README.md
